Thanks, [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] for reviewing this. I completely understand the need for transparency from a privacy perspective, but I wanted to flag a potential issue from a reclassification standpoint.

If we start informing drivers that they’ve been moved to the back of the queue for rejecting a certain number of trips, we’re essentially communicating that they’re being penalised for not accepting trips. This could be problematic because our Driver Terms and Conditions state:

{color:#4c9aff}*13.3. A Driver is free to:*{color}

{color:#4c9aff}*13.3.1. elect to fulfil or reject any offers to fulfil Journeys through the Driver App;*{color}

[~accountid:5d8df399c7d4e30dc2836580] If rejecting trips leads to consequences, then drivers are not truly "free" to decline trips without repercussions.

