It’s related to NUMA nodes info collection:

{noformat}		// On some Linux platforms(such as Arm64 guest kernel), cache info may not exist.
		// So, we should ignore error here.
		err = addCacheInfo(sysFs, &node) // addCacheInfo adds information about cache for NUMA node
		if err != nil {
			klog.V(1).Infof("Found node without cache information, nodeDir: %s", nodeDir)
		}{noformat}

According to logs, it got updated every 5 minutes. Don’t know why spike happens only once per 14min.

In Kubelet default caching interval is 2 minutes though [https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/kubelet/cadvisor/cadvisor_linux.go#L56|https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/kubelet/cadvisor/cadvisor_linux.go#L56|smart-link]  and I don’t see patches in EKS repo.

