Some issue with the current implementation of ProviderMetadataCache that might cause the event loop lag:

* when there is a large number of providers that need to be updated from the DB to the in-memory cache, this[ map operation|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/8c7f9bd64a3183ee032e752863aa6997c8f1423f/src/delivery/provider/delivery_provider/main/cache/ProviderMetadataCache.ts#L374-L378 ] is probably blocking the main thread causing ELL issues. This could be potentially mitigated by replacing it with a for loop + EventLoopDeferrer.defer() - [example|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/8c7f9bd64a3183ee032e752863aa6997c8f1423f/src/delivery/provider/delivery_provider/main/service/ProviderService.ts#L1197], [implementation|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-nodejs-common/blob/13f80aff46cbad5189ab1fd3ce2ce2830485375c/src/async/process/EventLoopDeferrer.ts#L29]
* in order to determine what providers to query from the DB to update in the cache, the *updatedSince* timestamp is used and compared to the last_update field from the Provider table. The *updatedSince* timestamp is updated [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/8c7f9bd64a3183ee032e752863aa6997c8f1423f/src/delivery/provider/delivery_provider/main/common/DataLoadingUtils.ts#L8] after the query in the DB. The predetermined value that is decremented from now() in order to account for the time it takes to run the query on the DB and not have missing data on the next run is configured [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/8c7f9bd64a3183ee032e752863aa6997c8f1423f/src/delivery/provider/delivery_provider/main/config/config.defaults.production.ts#L105] and is currently set to *10 minutes.* 
** That means that if there are a large number of providers that are updated at the same time/in a short span of time like in the cases analyzed in the previous comment, the cron will continuously query 6k+ providers from the DB every 5s for 10 minutes.
** As an alternative to the current implementation, one idea might be to do something similar to this in order to set updatedSince:

{noformat}const newUpdatedSince = now() - smallWindowBuffer;
ret = getIncrementalUpdate(this.updatedSince);
if(ret == success) {
	this.updatedSince = newUpdatedSince;
}{noformat}

